{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>You shall not plant yourself an asherah, etc.</b> Our Sages, may their memory be for blessing, said (Sanhedrin 7a): whoever appoints an unfit judge is as though he plants an asherah — end of quote. According to their words, Scripture said the word ״לְךָ״ to say that it is not counted against him as though, etc., but rather only if when he appoints him his intention is for some reason that concerns himself; but other than this, if he erred regarding an unfit judge and thought he was fit and appointed him, it is not counted against him as the planting of an asherah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:40.843954827Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}